---
// src/pages/vision.astro — The Vision
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import EmberMark from '../components/EmberMark.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import Reveal from '../components/Reveal.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';

const multiplying = [
  { title: 'Healthy leaders', body: 'strengthen healthy families.' },
  { title: 'Healthy families', body: 'strengthen churches, organizations, and communities.' },
  { title: 'Those communities', body: 'can influence regions and nations.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Vision"
  description="The founding vision of Ember Ridge: a house prepared for those who carry unusual responsibility — received without performance, restored in the presence of God, and sent back with clarity and endurance."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The Founding Vision"
    title="The Fire That Still Remains"
    lede="A house prepared for the Lord — and, out of that devotion, a place where those who carry His work are restored and sent back strengthened."
  />

  <EmberMark>
    An ember can appear small, buried, or nearly spent, yet it still holds living fire.
  </EmberMark>

  <Section tone="ivory" labelledby="first-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <Reveal>
        <SectionHeading
          id="first-heading"
          eyebrow="First, for the Lord"
          title="A house of worship before it is a house of restoration"
        />
      </Reveal>
      <Prose class="mt-12">
        <p>
          Ember Ridge exists first and foremost for the Lord. Before it is a place of
          restoration, it is a house of worship. We believe God has called us to
          purchase and cultivate this land in Moravian Falls — to saturate it in
          worship and intercession, to tend the fire of His presence day and night,
          and to serve Him with everything we are.
        </p>
        <p>
          Out of that devotion everything else flows: refreshing, reformation, and
          restoration for leaders, prophets, pastors, intercessors, and those carrying
          the weight of ministry. We are not building a ministry for people. We are
          building a house for the Lord, and He is inviting people to come.
        </p>
        <p>
          There are places built because an opportunity appears, and there are places
          prepared because a generation has reached a moment of need. Those who carry
          unusual responsibility will be received here without performance, restored in
          the presence of God, strengthened within healthy family life, and sent back
          into their callings with clarity and endurance.
        </p>
        <p>
          Across churches, ministries, schools, businesses, communities, and public
          life, faithful people are carrying burdens few others ever see. Many
          continue serving long after joy has been replaced by survival.
        </p>
      </Prose>


      <div class="mt-16">
        <Prose>
          <p>
            Ember Ridge will be a home devoted first to the Lord, where worship,
            prayer, Scripture, shared meals, honest relationships, rest, healing, and
            wise counsel create room for the Holy Spirit to work at a depth that
            scheduled gatherings rarely allow.
          </p>
        </Prose>


        <Prose>
          <p>
            The name carries the heart of the assignment. An ember can appear small,
            buried, or nearly spent, yet it still holds living fire. When protected,
            nourished, and given breath, it can burn brightly again. Ember Ridge exists
            to tend what He has already ignited — not to create identity, but to help
            restore strength, purity, joy, and obedience around it.
          </p>
        </Prose>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="linen" labelledby="multiplying-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <Reveal>
        <SectionHeading
          id="multiplying-heading"
          eyebrow="A Multiplying Vision"
          title="What God restores here is not meant to remain on the mountain"
          lede="This work is rooted in a multiplying vision."
        />
      </Reveal>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        {multiplying.map((m, i) => (
          <Reveal delay={i * 100}>
            <Card title={m.title}>
              <p>{m.body}</p>
            </Card>
          </Reveal>
        ))}
      </div>

      <Reveal delay="120" class="mt-14 max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed text-stone-700">
          People will return to their homes and assignments carrying renewed love for
          Christ, greater spiritual maturity, healthier relationships, clearer
          discernment, and a deeper capacity to serve.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-7">
          <a href="/ministry-model" class="btn-quiet">How the ministry model works →</a>
        </p>
      </Reveal>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <CTASection
    title="Take this vision before the Lord"
    body="We ask those who encounter this vision to ask whether God is inviting them to pray, build, give, serve, or connect the ministry with others who carry a corresponding assignment."
  />
</BaseLayout>
